 "notes": "Eddy-corner flats, slate-blue painted stucco (lifted to the lit tone), six storeys read off the street still: tall dark ground storey with a grilled shopfront left, a dark red frieze above it, three splayed bays (left, centre, right) up every upper storey, a railed steel fire escape right of centre, window pairs between. Ground right of the shop: small window, round-arched stone entry with a keystone between two columns (columns not modelled, surround only), then two windows. Cream trim, shallow cornice. Rework r-eddy: wall deepened to a mid steel blue (lit lum ~0.17), near-charcoal ground storey, red frieze with a thin gold line, white portal columns via hand.py. Tint lift (2026-10-02): paint tints lifted toward the sunlit paint (t' = 1-(1-t)k); brick tints converted to target / kit colour. Base fix (2026-10-03): cool/grey wallTint = target / painted-stucco base so the warm stucco albedo does not turn it pink. GroundBand lift (2026-10-03): groundBand tint #41444d -> #5e6068 (same rule as walls; it was missed by the first colour pass).",
